[#:seon.task{:name "a-deftest-reply-shows-only-its-var"
             :plan "Entering a deftest at the REPL answers #'ns/test-name and nothing else: no run, no pass/fail, no pending marker and no next operation, so the agent learns whether its regression is red or green only by proposing (dogfood loop 2026-09-28, loop 1: the proof's first verdict arrived 7 s later inside request-merge!'s refusal). The Var render of a test shows its status at its current reach digest (green, red with the first failing assertion, or pending) and offers the run of exactly that test, as the defn Var render shows reaching-test status. Read `seon.render.var/status` and `docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-loop-2026-09-28.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "reaching-tests-are-never-run-and-a-first-red-is-silent"
             :plan "The namespace docstring says a definition's batch schedules its reaching tests, but no pass does: the only callers of `seon.test/run` are `my.test/check`, `my.test/run-owned`, the retired request-merge! and root's candidate gate. Redefining a function reached by a test leaves status answering :pending across later passes with no member row. After an explicit `my.test/check` records that test red, status answers {} because a red with no earlier result is neither pending nor newly red, so the agent is never shown its red test. The pass schedules the reaching tests off the pass (agent-loop spec 4.5, AR-01) and status names a first red (AR-04). Read `seon.render.var/status` and `docs/seon/specs/agent-loop.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "the-offered-check-names-an-unquoted-symbol"
             :plan "A defn's reply offers (my.test/check {:seon.test/changed [my.program/source]}) with the symbol unquoted; agent fan-source ran it as offered and got \"my.test/check refused argument 0 at [:seon.test/changed 0]: expected ... a namespaced symbol, got an instance of clojure.lang.AFunction$1\" (fanout run, default e1a71b7c8, 2026-10-08). `seon.render.var/render-ai` builds (list 'my.test/check {:seon.test/changed [sym]}). Done when every offered operation evaluates as shown, with a test evaluating the offered form. Read `my.test/check`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-unchanged-redefinition-lists-pending-tests"
             :plan "Redefining `my.program-test/shown-value` with its exact text on a branch rendered `:seon.render.var/pending` with three reaching tests and a `my.test/check` operation, while `my.program/diff` showed no change to it (lane repl-only-a5, 2026-10-09). Done when the Var render of a definition at its base digest offers no pending tests. Read `seon.render.var/var-value?`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-malformed-contract-renders-as-missing"
             :plan "`seon.render.var` renders a definition whose authored contract Malli refuses (`:seon.fn/malformed-spec`) as `:seon.render.var/contract :missing` with the example `(defn f {:malli/schema [:=> [:cat :int] :int]} ...)`, while `seon.fn/contract-findings` now names it `:seon.fn.contract.finding/malformed-spec` with Malli's refusal (`:seon.fn.contract/malli-type`, `:seon.fn.contract/malli-data`, 6aa630885). Live run 11's program chain saw \"missing\" for 12 calls on a contract it had written. Render the malformed contract and Malli's refusal from the same finding (`seon.fn/contract-findings` for the one symbol). Proof: a Var render row of a function defined with `[:=> [:cat :vector] :int]` answers the malformed form and `:malli.core/child-error`."}
]
